-- Full content + SEO update for the three "Luxury Family Egypt" tours.
-- Changes duration, itinerary (day-by-day), the main description/"experience"
-- copy, includes/excludes, and SEO fields (title, seo_title,
-- meta_description, focus_keyword) for each. Slugs are preserved.
--
-- Meals rule applied across all three: Day 1 = Dinner only, the final
-- (departure) day = Breakfast only, every day in between = Breakfast, Lunch,
-- Dinner. The departure day also has no "accommodation" entry (the
-- itinerary JSON simply omits that key) since there's no hotel stay that
-- night — ItineraryDayCard.tsx only renders the accommodation row when the
-- field is present, so this cleanly hides it rather than showing a
-- placeholder like "N/A" next to the hotel icon.
--
-- lat/lng are real city-center coordinates for each stop (Giza, Cairo,
-- Luxor, Aswan, Alexandria, Siwa Oasis, Hurghada), matching the pattern
-- already used by other tours' itinerary JSON in this table.
--
-- seo_title kept under 60 characters and meta_description within 150-160,
-- per this project's SEO content convention.

UPDATE tours
SET
  title = '7-Day Family Tours Egypt: Cairo, Luxor & Aswan',
  duration = '7 Days / 6 Nights',
  description = 'Egypt has a rare gift for making history feel alive, and nowhere is that clearer than on a week built for the whole family. This family tours Egypt itinerary moves from the Great Pyramid of Giza to the temples of Luxor and the quiet Nile waters of Aswan, giving children and parents alike the space to stand before ancient monuments and ask questions no history book answers quite as vividly.

Each day is paced to hold a child''s attention without exhausting it, blending short educational stops with moments simply to look, wonder, and take in the scenery. A private guide and vehicle remove the friction of navigating a new country, so energy goes toward experiences rather than logistics.

A felucca sail on the Nile offers a natural pause between temple visits, while Nubian villages along the riverbank introduce a living culture alongside the ancient one. Families leave not just with photographs, but with stories from standing inside a pyramid together and watching their children fall in love with a civilization thousands of years old.',
  itinerary = '[{"day":1,"title":"Giza — Arrival and the Great Pyramid","description":"Your family''s journey begins in Giza with a private welcome and an unforgettable first encounter with the Great Pyramid of Khufu and the Great Sphinx. A private Egyptologist introduces the history behind Egypt''s most iconic monuments in a way that captures young imaginations, from the scale of ancient engineering to the myths surrounding the Sphinx. The Solar Boat Museum offers a quieter follow-up stop, revealing an ancient vessel built for a pharaoh''s journey to the afterlife. The day ends with rest, giving the family time to settle in before the week''s adventures begin.","activities":[],"lat":29.9792,"lng":31.1342,"placeName":"Giza, Egypt","meals":["Dinner"],"accommodation":"Marriott Mena House"},{"day":2,"title":"Cairo — The Egyptian Museum and Old Cairo","description":"A morning at the Egyptian Museum brings ancient Egypt''s treasures to life, including artifacts connected to Tutankhamun that fascinate children and adults alike. The afternoon shifts to Old Cairo, where the Hanging Church and Ben Ezra Synagogue reveal a different, layered side of the city''s history. A stroll through Khan el Khalili bazaar rounds out the day, giving the family a taste of Cairo''s everyday energy, color, and craftsmanship, a lively contrast to the morning''s quiet museum halls.","activities":[],"lat":30.0444,"lng":31.2357,"placeName":"Cairo, Egypt","meals":["Breakfast","Lunch","Dinner"],"accommodation":"Marriott Mena House"},{"day":3,"title":"Fly to Luxor — Karnak and Luxor Temple","description":"A short flight brings the family to Luxor, ancient Thebes, where the scale of Karnak Temple offers a dramatic introduction to New Kingdom Egypt. Towering columns and ancient hieroglyphics make for a memorable walk through history that photographs beautifully and sparks endless questions from younger travelers. In the evening, Luxor Temple takes on a different character entirely, its illuminated columns creating an atmospheric close to the day that feels distinctly different from the bright desert light of the morning''s exploration.","activities":[],"lat":25.6872,"lng":32.6396,"placeName":"Luxor, Egypt","meals":["Breakfast","Lunch","Dinner"],"accommodation":"Luxor"},{"day":4,"title":"Luxor West Bank — Valley of the Kings","description":"The West Bank of Luxor holds some of ancient Egypt''s most famous burial sites, and the Valley of the Kings offers children a chance to walk into real tombs decorated with vivid, well-preserved paintings. The Temple of Hatshepsut, rising in dramatic terraces from the cliffs, adds a striking architectural contrast to the underground tombs visited earlier. A private guide paces the visit to match the family''s energy, ensuring the day''s historical density never tips into exhaustion under the desert sun.","activities":[],"lat":25.6872,"lng":32.6396,"placeName":"Luxor, Egypt","meals":["Breakfast","Lunch","Dinner"],"accommodation":"Luxor"},{"day":5,"title":"Sail to Aswan — Kom Ombo and Edfu","description":"Traveling south toward Aswan, the family stops at two remarkable riverside temples along the way. Kom Ombo''s unique dual dedication to two ancient gods offers an interesting architectural puzzle, while Edfu Temple, remarkably well preserved, gives the clearest sense yet of what a complete ancient Egyptian temple once looked like. The gentle rhythm of river travel between stops offers welcome downtime, letting the Nile''s changing scenery become part of the day''s experience rather than simply transport between destinations.","activities":[],"lat":24.0889,"lng":32.8998,"placeName":"Aswan, Egypt","meals":["Breakfast","Lunch","Dinner"],"accommodation":"Sofitel Legend Old Cataract"},{"day":6,"title":"Aswan — Nile Felucca and Nubian Village","description":"Aswan''s slower pace offers a natural breathing room after days of temple exploration. A traditional felucca sail across the Nile introduces the family to the river''s quieter beauty, while a visit to a Nubian village adds a living cultural dimension alongside the ancient history explored earlier in the week. Bright, hand-painted homes and warm local hospitality give children a memorable contrast to temples and tombs, rounding out the trip''s cultural range before the return journey begins.","activities":[],"lat":24.0889,"lng":32.8998,"placeName":"Aswan, Egypt","meals":["Breakfast","Lunch","Dinner"],"accommodation":"Sofitel Legend Old Cataract"},{"day":7,"title":"Fly to Cairo — Departure","description":"A morning flight returns the family to Cairo, where remaining time can be used for last-minute exploration or simply relaxing before departure. A private transfer to the airport closes out the week smoothly, bringing a journey that spanned five thousand years of history to a comfortable and unhurried end. Children leave with more than souvenirs, carrying home real memories of pyramids, temples, and a river that connects it all together.","activities":[],"lat":30.0444,"lng":31.2357,"placeName":"Cairo, Egypt","meals":["Breakfast"]}]'::jsonb,
  includes = ARRAY['6 nights luxury 5-star accommodation', 'All meals daily (breakfast, lunch, and dinner)', 'Private licensed Egyptologist guide throughout', 'Internal domestic flights (Cairo–Luxor, Aswan–Cairo)', 'All private transfers in air-conditioned vehicles', 'Private entry and guided access to all listed archaeological sites', 'Traditional felucca sail on the Nile in Aswan', 'Gratuities for guides and drivers', '24/7 concierge contact throughout your journey']::text[],
  excludes = ARRAY['International flights', 'Egypt entry visa', 'Travel insurance', 'Personal expenses', 'Optional activities not mentioned in the itinerary', 'Any items not specifically listed above']::text[],
  focus_keyword = 'family tours egypt',
  seo_title = 'Family Tours Egypt | 7-Day Cairo, Luxor & Aswan Tour',
  meta_description = 'Explore the best family tours Egypt has to offer on this 7-day journey through Cairo, Luxor, and Aswan, with private guides and five-star comfort throughout.'
WHERE slug = '10-day-egypt-family-tour';

UPDATE tours
SET
  title = '10-Day Egypt Family Vacation Packages: Nile & Red Sea',
  duration = '10 Days / 9 Nights',
  description = 'Ten days gives a family the rare luxury of time, enough to explore Egypt''s ancient wonders without rushing and still leave room to unwind by the Red Sea. This egypt family vacation packages itinerary carries families from the pyramids of Giza through the temples of Luxor and Aswan, then west to the warm waters of Hurghada for a few days of pure relaxation before returning to Cairo.

Children experience history not as something read about but as something walked through, standing inside temples built thousands of years ago and sailing waters that once carried pharaohs. The pacing allows for real rest between cultural stops, avoiding the exhaustion that shorter, more compressed itineraries often bring to younger travelers.

By blending ancient sites with beach days, this journey gives every member of the family something to look forward to each morning, whether that means exploring a tomb or simply floating in the Red Sea. Ten days proves long enough to see Egypt properly, and short enough to keep everyone excited until the final day.',
  itinerary = '[{"day":1,"title":"Giza — Arrival and the Great Pyramid","description":"Your family''s journey begins in Giza with a private welcome and an unforgettable first encounter with the Great Pyramid of Khufu and the Great Sphinx. A private Egyptologist introduces the history behind Egypt''s most iconic monuments in a way that captures young imaginations, from the scale of ancient engineering to the myths surrounding the Sphinx. The Solar Boat Museum offers a quieter follow-up stop, revealing an ancient vessel built for a pharaoh''s journey to the afterlife.","activities":[],"lat":29.9792,"lng":31.1342,"placeName":"Giza, Egypt","meals":["Dinner"],"accommodation":"Marriott Mena House"},{"day":2,"title":"Cairo — The Egyptian Museum and Old Cairo","description":"A morning at the Egyptian Museum brings ancient Egypt''s treasures to life, including artifacts connected to Tutankhamun that fascinate children and adults alike. The afternoon shifts to Old Cairo, where the Hanging Church and Ben Ezra Synagogue reveal a different, layered side of the city''s history. A stroll through Khan el Khalili bazaar rounds out the day with color and everyday local life.","activities":[],"lat":30.0444,"lng":31.2357,"placeName":"Cairo, Egypt","meals":["Breakfast","Lunch","Dinner"],"accommodation":"Marriott Mena House"},{"day":3,"title":"Saqqara and Dahshur — Beyond Giza","description":"Before heading south, the family explores Saqqara''s Step Pyramid, the world''s oldest monumental stone structure, followed by the Bent and Red Pyramids at Dahshur. These lesser visited sites offer a quieter, more personal encounter with pyramid building''s earliest chapters, giving children a deeper sense of how the Great Pyramid came to be.","activities":[],"lat":30.0444,"lng":31.2357,"placeName":"Cairo, Egypt","meals":["Breakfast","Lunch","Dinner"],"accommodation":"Marriott Mena House"},{"day":4,"title":"Fly to Luxor — Karnak and Luxor Temple","description":"A short flight brings the family to Luxor, ancient Thebes, where the scale of Karnak Temple offers a dramatic introduction to New Kingdom Egypt. In the evening, Luxor Temple takes on a different character entirely, its illuminated columns creating an atmospheric close to the day.","activities":[],"lat":25.6872,"lng":32.6396,"placeName":"Luxor, Egypt","meals":["Breakfast","Lunch","Dinner"],"accommodation":"Luxor"},{"day":5,"title":"Luxor West Bank — Valley of the Kings","description":"The West Bank of Luxor holds some of ancient Egypt''s most famous burial sites, and the Valley of the Kings offers children a chance to walk into real tombs decorated with vivid, well-preserved paintings. The Temple of Hatshepsut adds a striking architectural contrast rising in terraces from the cliffs.","activities":[],"lat":25.6872,"lng":32.6396,"placeName":"Luxor, Egypt","meals":["Breakfast","Lunch","Dinner"],"accommodation":"Luxor"},{"day":6,"title":"Sail to Aswan — Kom Ombo and Edfu","description":"Traveling south toward Aswan, the family stops at Kom Ombo, uniquely dedicated to two ancient gods, and Edfu, remarkably well preserved. The gentle rhythm of river travel between stops offers welcome downtime, letting the Nile''s changing scenery become part of the day.","activities":[],"lat":24.0889,"lng":32.8998,"placeName":"Aswan, Egypt","meals":["Breakfast","Lunch","Dinner"],"accommodation":"Sofitel Legend Old Cataract"},{"day":7,"title":"Aswan — Nile Felucca and Nubian Village","description":"Aswan''s slower pace offers natural breathing room after days of temple exploration. A traditional felucca sail across the Nile introduces the family to the river''s quieter beauty, while a Nubian village visit adds a living cultural dimension alongside the ancient history.","activities":[],"lat":24.0889,"lng":32.8998,"placeName":"Aswan, Egypt","meals":["Breakfast","Lunch","Dinner"],"accommodation":"Sofitel Legend Old Cataract"},{"day":8,"title":"Fly to Hurghada — Red Sea Arrival","description":"A short flight carries the family from ancient temples to the turquoise waters of the Red Sea. The afternoon is left open for the family to settle into their beachfront resort, unwind by the pool, and enjoy their first taste of Hurghada''s relaxed coastal pace after days of cultural exploration.","activities":[],"lat":27.2579,"lng":33.8116,"placeName":"Hurghada, Egypt","meals":["Breakfast","Lunch","Dinner"],"accommodation":"Hurghada"},{"day":9,"title":"Hurghada — Red Sea Relaxation","description":"A full day by the Red Sea gives the family time to simply rest, swim, and enjoy resort facilities together. For families wanting more activity, a gentle snorkeling excursion or boat trip to nearby reefs offers an easy, family-friendly introduction to Egypt''s marine life, a fitting contrast to the week''s earlier history-focused days.","activities":[],"lat":27.2579,"lng":33.8116,"placeName":"Hurghada, Egypt","meals":["Breakfast","Lunch","Dinner"],"accommodation":"Hurghada"},{"day":10,"title":"Fly to Cairo — Departure","description":"A morning flight returns the family to Cairo, where remaining time can be used for last-minute exploration or simply relaxing before departure. A private transfer to the airport closes out the ten days smoothly, bringing a journey that spanned ancient temples and Red Sea shores to a comfortable end.","activities":[],"lat":30.0444,"lng":31.2357,"placeName":"Cairo, Egypt","meals":["Breakfast"]}]'::jsonb,
  includes = ARRAY['9 nights luxury 5-star accommodation', 'All meals daily (breakfast, lunch, and dinner)', 'Private licensed Egyptologist guide throughout', 'Internal domestic flights (Cairo–Luxor, Aswan–Hurghada, Hurghada–Cairo)', 'All private transfers in air-conditioned vehicles', 'Private entry and guided access to all listed archaeological sites', 'Traditional felucca sail on the Nile in Aswan', 'Gratuities for guides and drivers', '24/7 concierge contact throughout your journey']::text[],
  excludes = ARRAY['International flights', 'Egypt entry visa', 'Travel insurance', 'Personal expenses', 'Optional activities not mentioned in the itinerary', 'Any items not specifically listed above']::text[],
  focus_keyword = 'egypt family vacation packages',
  seo_title = 'Egypt Family Vacation Packages | 10-Day Nile & Red Sea Tour',
  meta_description = 'Discover Egypt family vacation packages combining ancient temples along the Nile with relaxing days by the Red Sea, all in one private 10-day journey.'
WHERE slug = 'egypt-luxury-family-tour';

UPDATE tours
SET
  title = '12-Day Egypt Tours Family: Alexandria, Nile & Siwa',
  duration = '12 Days / 11 Nights',
  description = 'Twelve days transforms an Egypt family trip from a highlights tour into a genuine journey through the country''s full range, from Mediterranean shores to ancient temples and finally the silence of the Western Desert. This egypt tours family itinerary begins at the pyramids of Giza, travels north to cosmopolitan Alexandria, south through the temples of Luxor and Aswan, and west into the remote beauty of Siwa Oasis before returning to Cairo.

This is not a repeat of Egypt''s most familiar postcard images stretched over more days, but a deliberately varied journey that gives children a fuller picture of the country, its Mediterranean history, its pharaonic monuments, and its desert culture, all within a single family trip. Each region offers a different rhythm, keeping the itinerary fresh even for children who tire easily of repetition.

By the journey''s end, families have touched nearly every corner of Egypt''s character, from ancient tombs to salt lakes shimmering in the desert sun. Twelve days proves long enough to make Egypt feel fully explored rather than merely visited, a rare achievement for a single family vacation.',
  itinerary = '[{"day":1,"title":"Giza — Arrival and the Great Pyramid","description":"Your family''s journey begins in Giza with a private welcome and an unforgettable first encounter with the Great Pyramid of Khufu and the Great Sphinx. A private Egyptologist introduces the history behind Egypt''s most iconic monuments in a way that captures young imaginations. The Solar Boat Museum offers a quieter follow-up stop nearby.","activities":[],"lat":29.9792,"lng":31.1342,"placeName":"Giza, Egypt","meals":["Dinner"],"accommodation":"Marriott Mena House"},{"day":2,"title":"Cairo — The Egyptian Museum and Old Cairo","description":"A morning at the Egyptian Museum brings ancient Egypt''s treasures to life, including artifacts connected to Tutankhamun. The afternoon shifts to Old Cairo, where the Hanging Church and Ben Ezra Synagogue reveal a different, layered side of the city''s history, followed by a stroll through Khan el Khalili bazaar.","activities":[],"lat":30.0444,"lng":31.2357,"placeName":"Cairo, Egypt","meals":["Breakfast","Lunch","Dinner"],"accommodation":"Marriott Mena House"},{"day":3,"title":"Drive to Alexandria — Mediterranean Egypt","description":"A scenic drive north brings the family to Alexandria, a city facing the Mediterranean rather than the Nile. Qaitbay Citadel, built on the site of the ancient Lighthouse, offers a striking seaside introduction, while the modern Bibliotheca Alexandrina connects the city''s ancient intellectual legacy to the present day.","activities":[],"lat":31.2001,"lng":29.9187,"placeName":"Alexandria, Egypt","meals":["Breakfast","Lunch","Dinner"],"accommodation":"Alexandria"},{"day":4,"title":"Alexandria — Catacombs and Return to Cairo","description":"The morning explores the Catacombs of Kom el Shoqafa, Egypt''s largest Roman funerary complex, offering a mysterious underground contrast to the previous day''s coastal views. The family then returns to Cairo by road, with time to rest before continuing south the following day.","activities":[],"lat":31.2001,"lng":29.9187,"placeName":"Alexandria, Egypt","meals":["Breakfast","Lunch","Dinner"],"accommodation":"Cairo"},{"day":5,"title":"Fly to Luxor — Karnak and Luxor Temple","description":"A short flight brings the family to Luxor, ancient Thebes, where the scale of Karnak Temple offers a dramatic introduction to New Kingdom Egypt. In the evening, Luxor Temple takes on a different character entirely, its illuminated columns creating an atmospheric close to the day.","activities":[],"lat":25.6872,"lng":32.6396,"placeName":"Luxor, Egypt","meals":["Breakfast","Lunch","Dinner"],"accommodation":"Luxor"},{"day":6,"title":"Luxor West Bank — Valley of the Kings","description":"The West Bank of Luxor holds some of ancient Egypt''s most famous burial sites, and the Valley of the Kings offers children a chance to walk into real tombs decorated with vivid, well-preserved paintings. The Temple of Hatshepsut adds a striking architectural contrast rising in terraces from the cliffs.","activities":[],"lat":25.6872,"lng":32.6396,"placeName":"Luxor, Egypt","meals":["Breakfast","Lunch","Dinner"],"accommodation":"Luxor"},{"day":7,"title":"Sail to Aswan — Kom Ombo and Edfu","description":"Traveling south toward Aswan, the family stops at Kom Ombo, uniquely dedicated to two ancient gods, and Edfu, remarkably well preserved. The gentle rhythm of river travel between stops offers welcome downtime along the Nile.","activities":[],"lat":24.0889,"lng":32.8998,"placeName":"Aswan, Egypt","meals":["Breakfast","Lunch","Dinner"],"accommodation":"Sofitel Legend Old Cataract"},{"day":8,"title":"Aswan — Nile Felucca and Nubian Village","description":"Aswan''s slower pace offers natural breathing room after days of temple exploration. A traditional felucca sail across the Nile introduces the family to the river''s quieter beauty, while a Nubian village visit adds a living cultural dimension alongside the ancient history.","activities":[],"lat":24.0889,"lng":32.8998,"placeName":"Aswan, Egypt","meals":["Breakfast","Lunch","Dinner"],"accommodation":"Sofitel Legend Old Cataract"},{"day":9,"title":"Fly to Cairo, Drive to Siwa — Desert Arrival","description":"The family flies back to Cairo before driving deep into the Western Desert toward Siwa Oasis. The long drive itself becomes part of the adventure, as the landscape shifts dramatically from the Nile Valley to endless desert. Arrival in Siwa offers a completely different atmosphere from the rest of the journey.","activities":[],"lat":29.2032,"lng":25.5196,"placeName":"Siwa Oasis, Egypt","meals":["Breakfast","Lunch","Dinner"],"accommodation":"Siwa Oasis"},{"day":10,"title":"Siwa — Temple of the Oracle and Shali Fortress","description":"Siwa''s ancient Temple of the Oracle once drew Alexander the Great across the desert, and the family follows that same sense of discovery today. Shali Fortress, built entirely from local salt rock and mud, offers a striking contrast to the stone temples explored earlier in the journey.","activities":[],"lat":29.2032,"lng":25.5196,"placeName":"Siwa Oasis, Egypt","meals":["Breakfast","Lunch","Dinner"],"accommodation":"Siwa Oasis"},{"day":11,"title":"Siwa — Cleopatra''s Bath and Return to Cairo","description":"A morning visit to Cleopatra''s Bath, a natural spring said to have once drawn the queen herself, offers a relaxed final stop in Siwa. The family then makes the return drive to Cairo, arriving in the evening with time to rest before departure.","activities":[],"lat":29.2032,"lng":25.5196,"placeName":"Siwa Oasis, Egypt","meals":["Breakfast","Lunch","Dinner"],"accommodation":"Cairo"},{"day":12,"title":"Cairo — Departure","description":"The final morning allows time for last-minute exploration or simply relaxing before departure. A private transfer to the airport closes out the twelve days smoothly, bringing a journey that spanned Mediterranean shores, ancient temples, and desert oases to a comfortable end.","activities":[],"lat":30.0444,"lng":31.2357,"placeName":"Cairo, Egypt","meals":["Breakfast"]}]'::jsonb,
  includes = ARRAY['11 nights luxury 5-star accommodation', 'All meals daily (breakfast, lunch, and dinner)', 'Private licensed Egyptologist guide throughout', 'Internal domestic flights (Cairo–Luxor)', 'All private transfers in air-conditioned vehicles', 'Private entry and guided access to all listed archaeological sites', 'Traditional felucca sail on the Nile in Aswan', 'Gratuities for guides and drivers', '24/7 concierge contact throughout your journey']::text[],
  excludes = ARRAY['International flights', 'Egypt entry visa', 'Travel insurance', 'Personal expenses', 'Optional activities not mentioned in the itinerary', 'Any items not specifically listed above']::text[],
  focus_keyword = 'egypt tours family',
  seo_title = 'Egypt Tours Family | 12-Day Alexandria, Nile & Siwa Journey',
  meta_description = 'These egypt tours family itineraries cover Alexandria coast, Nile Valley temples, and Siwa Oasis over 12 unforgettable days for the whole family to enjoy.'
WHERE slug = '14-day-egypt-family-tour';
